Second Attempt:

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:42.400
<i>Thank goodness.
 I came out pretty well.</i>

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.140
Nice job, Irido-san!

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:45.800
On to the next one!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:46.880
Right.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.880
<b>Grip Strength</b>

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.880
<b>Left</b>

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.880
<b>Average</b>

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.880
<b>Right</b>

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.390
<b>Sit-ups</b>

00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:59.890
<b>Sit and Reach</b>

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.400
<b>Standing Long Jump</b>

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.900
<b>Handball Throw</b>

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.910
<b>50m Dash</b>

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:22.270
Let's go, Irido-san!

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:23.140
Okay...

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:28.920
On your marks...

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:36.000
<i>Come on. This doesn't suck for her one bit.</i>

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.040
<i>You can never trust a girl!</i>

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.560
Minami-san, 7.3 seconds.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.600
Irido-san, 8.5 seconds.

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.570
Nice job, Irido-san!

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:54.300
You too... Minami-san...

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.210
You did good.

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:08.960
But I think you've pushed yourself enough.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.430
A-Are you all right?!

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.430
Hey—Whoa there!

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:18.810
She's in your hands.

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:23.880
Why is Irido-kun still out here?

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:27.480
I thought the boys were done 
with the outdoor stuff.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.490
<b>Nurse's Office</b>

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:38.120
I'm sorry I didn't realize you 
were so worn out, Irido-san.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:39.580
No, it's okay.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:43.710
It was my own fault for trying 
so hard in the first place.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:45.500
Trying so hard?

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.630
I'm actually really bad at athletics.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:52.300
I was worried people would find out,

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:54.260
so I've been staying up late weight training

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:56.760
and reading books on sports 
from cover to cover.

00:08:57.210 --> 00:09:00.400
I think I just wore myself 
out from lack of sleep.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:01.980
Gotcha.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:06.280
That makes me feel so much closer to you!

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:08.020
Huh? Why is that?

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:12.800
If I'm honest, part of me found 
you a little hard to approach.

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:16.620
I mean, you're pretty and smart. 
Out of my league, in a way.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:18.620
But man, I had no idea.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:21.500
So you suck at sports and 
you're a try-hard, huh?

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:25.910
N-Now you're getting under my skin. 
Mind if I let you have it?

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:26.940
Go right ahead.

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:28.920
I'd love to see you when you're angry.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:31.860
Well then, sorry in advance.

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:33.580
H-Hey, you...

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:39.450
"Hey, you," she says! You're so cute!

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:44.810
D-Don't laugh. You're making 
me feel self-conscious.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.910
Hey, Irido-san!

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:49.310
Is it all right if I call you Yume-chan?

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:52.320
Huh? Y-You mean by my given name?

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:55.070
Yeah, exactly! Is that cool?

00:09:55.070 --> 00:10:01.580
Um, sure. I m-mean... I'd like that.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:03.390
Hurray!

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:06.550
I'm so glad we're friends now, Yume-chan!

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:13.260
<i>Wait, does this mean I have 
to call her by her name now too?!</i>

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:19.060
A-A-Aka... Akatsu...

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:22.830
There, there. You can take your time.

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:24.470
There's no need to rush.

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:29.730
It's a pleasure to get to know you
 as well, Minami-san.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:32.990
Hold on. So you're not gonna call me Akatsuki?

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:34.480
And why so formal?!

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:50.140
Um, about earlier...

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:51.720
You've got bags under your eyes.

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:53.170
What?! No way!

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:57.000
I was kidding.

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:01.210
<i>What an insufferable jerk!</i>

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:04.350
<i>I can't believe he saw through my 
attempts to look good this whole time!</i>

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:08.100
Irido-kun's so sweet when 
it comes to you, Yume-chan.

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:09.960
Huh?! What makes you think <i>that</i>?!

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:11.060
Hmm?

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:13.190
Oh, I dunno...

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:19.030
<b>My Stepmom's Daughter Is My Ex</b>

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:21.030
School Motto
Work Diligently. Think Critically.
Strive for Excellence. Take Initiative.

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:21.030
What?!

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:24.030
Yume's out sick with a fever?!

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:26.030
Is she okay?! What's her temperature?!

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:28.080
Thirty-eight degrees, apparently.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:30.120
Thirty-eight degrees?!

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:34.360
Settle down, Minami. You're weirding him out.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:37.630
Hey! Quit holding me like I'm a cat.

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:38.830
Right, right.

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:39.800
Me—ow!

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.460
What's your problem, Kawanami?

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:45.930
My good friend's being harassed
 by some weirdo, so I had to step in.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:47.210
Huh?

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:49.440
Aren't you just getting 
buddy-buddy with Irido-kun

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:52.520
in order to get closer to Yume-chan?

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:54.310
Kinda creepy if you ask me.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:56.560
Don't worry yourself about that.

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:59.070
When it comes to love, 
I'm but a lurker in chat.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:01.570
A lurker in chat? 
What's that supposed to mean?

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:05.070
I never participate. 
I merely watch things unfold.

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:08.030
It's far more enjoyable that way.

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:10.880
Oh, so you're a peeping Tom.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:11.840
Wait!

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:14.040
But none of that matters!

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:17.800
I've made up my mind! I'm gonna go see 
how she's doing after school!

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:18.800
What?

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:22.350
Could you maybe look 
a <i>little</i> less put out?

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:24.320
That <i>does</i> sound like fun.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:25.290
Count me in too!

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:27.100
You won't be necessary, Kawanami.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:28.310
And why not?!

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:29.910
See ya!

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:30.670
Yeah, see you tomorrow!

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:32.310
Stay safe!

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:37.530
So you and Yume-chan were complete 
strangers before last year, right?

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:42.320
Was it hard becoming siblings 
and moving in together so suddenly?

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:46.120
Well, it's the kind of thing 
that gets easier with time.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:47.820
Though there <i>are</i> points of concern.

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:52.200
Open 24 Hours

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:49.610
Right?!

00:12:49.610 --> 00:12:52.200
Like accidentally walking in
 on each other changing?

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:56.120
We're both doing our best to avoid that.

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:58.650
Aw, how boring.

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:01.880
Whoa!

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:04.570
So this is where you live, Irido-kun?

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:06.410
Just so we're clear,

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:09.640
you showing up out of the blue
 will probably surprise her,

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:11.140
so rein it in, will you?

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:14.770
Aw, but the whole point was to surprise her.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.340
People who are sick don't need surprises.

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:33.900
I'm coming in.

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:45.430
She's conked out, huh?

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:46.130
Seems so.

00:13:57.620 --> 00:14:00.150
Irido-kun...

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:03.900
H-Hey... How are you feeling?

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:09.150
Where have you been? I was lonely.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.950
U-Um...

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:15.660
L-Look! Minami-san's here to see you.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:18.670
Hey, Yume-chan. How're you doing?

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:21.800
To see me...?

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:30.550
How's the fever? Still pretty bad?

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:33.440
Thanks for checking up on me, Minami-san.

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:36.060
My fever's already gone done quite a bit.

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:39.260
Hey, are you feeling 
hungry at all, Yume-chan?

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:42.380
I bought stuff to make you some rice porridge!

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:43.820
Come help me, Irido-kun.

00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:48.490
You're a decent cook, aren't you?
 Yume-chan told me so.

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:55.230
So, I've been thinking...

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:57.830
Isn't it going to be difficult for you now?

00:14:58.090 --> 00:14:59.330
What?

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:01.710
What'll you do if you get a girlfriend?

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:03.340
Bringing her over will be hard, right?

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:04.800
Huh?

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:07.710
Do I look like the kind of guy
 who can get a girl?

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:11.470
Well, you've already had one, 
haven't you, Irido-kun?

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:17.350
I've kinda got a knack for 
picking up on that stuff, y'know?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:20.060
Like how you interact with girls.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:24.230
I was like, "Yeah, this guy's 
probably had a girlfriend before."

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:26.670
But not anymore, right?

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:28.490
Well? Hit the nail on the head?

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:29.880
No comment.

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:32.360
Oh, so you're taking that route.

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:35.370
But really, what'll you do 
if you get another girl?

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:38.370
Highly unlikely. Besides, I don't want one.

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:41.870
I'm saying <i>if</i>. You wouldn't 
introduce her to Yume-chan?

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:45.900
Of course not.
 It's not like I need her blessing.

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:47.000
And it'd be a pain.

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:52.380
But that means she'd never find out
 if you have someone or not.

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:54.410
Unless you got married.

00:15:54.410 --> 00:15:56.180
I guess not.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:16:00.360
I see, I see. Very interesting.

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:05.650
Well, that should be good.

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:09.150
All right, Yume-chan. Say, "Ahh!"

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:11.740
I-I can feed myself, you know?

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:14.480
Not a chance. You're sick!

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:16.240
Now, open up!

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:24.250
Well? Do you like it?

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:29.250
Really?! What a relief!

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:30.510
Now, one more bite!

00:16:29.970 --> 00:16:33.380
<i>What am I even watching here?</i>

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:35.470
Tell her I said to get better soon.

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:37.390
Yeah, I'll pass it on.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:40.270
Hey, can I ask you something?

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:41.270
<b>Irido</b>

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:45.520
You and Yume-chan are just siblings, right?

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.020
Yup, that's right. Stepsiblings.

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:52.060
Oh! Stepsiblings, huh?

00:16:52.060 --> 00:16:54.780
Not <i>just</i> siblings then. Gotcha, gotcha.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:57.280
<b>Irido</b>

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:57.280
Welp, I'll see you later!

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:07.170
Minami-san's gone home now.

00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:12.520
Well, aren't the two of you
 getting along nicely...

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:16.230
Making rice porridge together like that.

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:18.560
So we're perfectly clear,

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:21.500
that remark just now meant,

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:26.690
"I hate seeing my dear friend with
 a good-for-nothing loser like you," correct?

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:29.790
Yeah... You got it.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:31.130
Honestly...

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:35.420
Listen, Minami-san's just outgoing.

00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:41.420
People like her naturally tend
 to get along with anyone and everyone.

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:44.200
Though that might be hard to grasp
 for someone reinventing themselves.

00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:47.540
I'm not... doing that...

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:50.190
Get some sleep.

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:53.470
If you want to get better, you need to rest.

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:55.970
Are you... gonna leave me again?

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:58.930
I'm not going anywhere. 
I'm staying home today.

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:03.810
Liar. You left the last time...

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:06.730
The last time? What do you mean?

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:10.630
Even though I asked you to hold my hand...

00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:13.610
When I woke up, you were gone.

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:19.610
Honestly, does your brain just get sent 
back in time whenever you catch a cold?

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.390
Here.

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:24.870
I won't let go this time, 
so try to go to sleep, okay?

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:34.880
Thank you, Irido-kun...

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:41.390
<b>April</b>

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:45.640
<i>Looking back, I can only describe 
it as a youthful indiscretion.</i>

00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:49.450
<i>But from seventh to eighth grade,</i>

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:52.650
<i>I had what you might call a girlfriend.</i>

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:56.660
<i>Her name was Ayai Yume.</i>

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:00.660
<i>At least, it was at the time.</i>

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:03.660
<i>We read books and talked about them together.</i>

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:05.930
<i>And when she got sick, I'd hold her hand.</i>

00:19:06.990 --> 00:19:10.670
<i>Like some couple out of a YA novel
 for love-obsessed teens,</i>

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:12.820
<i>we spent our days never tiring of one another.</i>

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:16.170
<i>But trivial disagreements began to pile up,</i>

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:18.670
<i>and by graduation,
 we went our separate ways.</i>

00:19:19.110 --> 00:19:22.730
<i>It was a perfectly typical romance,</i>

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:24.680
<i>until that day...</i>

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:27.680
<i>My dad had gotten remarried,</i>

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:30.810
<i>and the moment I came face-to-face 
with my stepmom's daughter,</i>

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:32.760
<i>only one thought crossed my mind.</i>

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:37.100
<i>And I'm sure she was thinking 
the exact same thing.</i>

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:41.700
<i>"God's a real comedian."</i>

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:45.700
<b>April</b>

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:45.260
Hey.

00:19:46.150 --> 00:19:47.700
I'm thirsty.

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:49.200
Don't spill it.

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:51.210
Go buy me ice cream.

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:52.670
What kind?

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:54.920
I want a book. Gimme money.

00:19:55.280 --> 00:19:56.380
Why should I?

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:59.510
Would you... hold my hand again?

00:20:00.370 --> 00:20:01.850
Yeah, yeah.

00:20:02.740 --> 00:20:03.630
Hey.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:06.010
It's time to check your temperature again.

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:09.210
If you've been resting all day 
and it still hasn't gone down,

00:20:09.210 --> 00:20:11.520
then it could be serious, you know?

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:15.480
N-No, I'm okay! I'm completely fine!

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:19.540
We need to take your temperature 
to make sure, don't we?

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:22.520
Now raise your arm.

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:23.860
N-No...

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:27.290
<i>No</i>!

00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:31.900
It's 36.5 degrees...

00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:39.880
All right, you. How long 
has your fever been gone?

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:42.380
No comment.

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:46.220
You weren't pretending to be sick
just to boss me around, were you?

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:48.220
No comment!

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:52.140
So asking me to hold your hand was also...

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:55.080
Hey, don't you run away!

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:58.110
I'm going back to sleep just to be safe!

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:00.090
You've slept enough, haven't you?

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:02.110
Taking advantage of my kindness like that!

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:09.330
Don't you have something to say?

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:12.330
Um...

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:16.330
Or can you not say it unless 
I hold your hand for you?

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:21.090
I-I'm sorry for pretending to be sick.

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:23.690
Very good.

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:27.100
Well, it's true that you're 
still technically recovering,

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:29.100
so I'll let it slide this time.

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:33.100
You being nice to me is weirding me out.

00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:35.580
I'll take that as a compliment,

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:38.600
Miss I Can't Fall Asleep 
Without You Holding My Hand.

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:42.990
I can't hear you!

00:21:42.990 --> 00:21:44.990
I have no idea what you're talking about!

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:49.640
If you're this lively, I guess you 
don't need me to look after you anymore.

00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:51.440
I'm going back to my room now, okay?

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:52.090
Hey...

00:21:52.090 --> 00:21:52.830
Hmm?

00:21:53.230 --> 00:21:54.970
Don't go off somewhere...

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:57.000
and leave me behind.

00:21:58.350 --> 00:22:01.250
Well, we are siblings now.

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:06.010
I think I can stick around.
